{"descent":["An imprimitive character differs from its primitive inducing character by finitely many Euler factors, none of which vanishes for ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{Re}s&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>"},"."],"residues":["The Mellin transform of a ramp is ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n^{-s}/(s(s-1))</annotation></semantics></math>"},"; a zero of any family member becomes a pole whose residue cannot be cancelled, because the weights are positive."],"criterion":["If a positive family's prime sum stays below ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Cy^\\theta</annotation></semantics></math>"}," throughout arbitrarily late windows ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[Y,Y^{1+\\delta}]</annotation></semantics></math>"},", none of its ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math>"},"-functions vanishes to the right of ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\theta</annotation></semantics></math>"},"."],"choreography":["The loss exponents are fixed first; given a zero with ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta&gt;\\tfrac12</annotation></semantics></math>"}," choose ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\theta\\in(\\tfrac12,\\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>"},", then ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>"}," with ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tfrac12+9\\varepsilon\\le\\theta</annotation></semantics></math>"},". No bound at ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varepsilon=0</annotation></semantics></math>"}," is ever needed."],"comparison":["Finite Fourier orthogonality on a subgroup and an exact main-term identity convert a geometric discrepancy bound into the prime-sum bound, with exponent ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\" displaystyle=\"false\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\tfrac12+(e_D+e_L+7)\\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>"},"."],"family":["A chain of about ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt x</annotation></semantics></math>"}," theta lifts, with divisibility, slope and covolume control, is chosen so that both loss exponents are fixed numbers: ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_D=2</annotation></semantics></math>"},", ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e_L=0</annotation></semantics></math>"},"."],"hosts":["For each primitive character ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\psi</annotation></semantics></math>"},", the cohomological window produces arithmetic hosts of width ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3/2</annotation></semantics></math>"}," at all large scales of a system of scales."],"cohomology":["On a whole interval ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">[Y,Y^2]</annotation></semantics></math>"},", weighted lengths of locally trivial Galois cohomology of twisted modules are at most ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sqrt{\\exp(x^{\\varepsilon})}</annotation></semantics></math>"},", uniformly over the relevant fields."],"galois":["For regular algebraic polarized cuspidal ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>"}," on ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mrow><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{GL}_a</annotation></semantics></math>"}," over a CM field, a continuous semisimple ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\ell</annotation></semantics></math>"},"-adic representation whose Frobenius polynomials match the Satake parameters of ",{"math":"<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi</annotation></semantics></math>"},"."]}
